{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VadYuhUaWqVUQuTrU5PKvB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context. Let me now dispatch two reviewers in parallel following the dream-review-full dispatch template:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nI'll launch them as parallel agents, then conduct the roundtable process.\n\nLet me first summarize what I've learned from the paper:\n\n**Title:** Temporal Label Models for Estimating Progress in LLM Agent Trajectories\n\n**Key contributions:**\n1. Temporal Label Model (TLM) - HMM-based aggregation that models LF temporal dynamics (leading/concurrent/lagging roles), improving label quality by 12.2pp over MV and 5.9pp over FlyingSquid on a human gold set (κ=0.82)\n\n\n2. ProgressProbe - a lightweight GRU probe trained on TLM labels that achieves 0.858 macro-F1 on the gold set, beating the LF oracle by 6.0pp and outperforming Claude Sonnet CoT by 4.5pp while running 690× faster\n3. Cross-agent transferability - the probe generalizes well across agents, retaining 0.791 F1 when transferred from SWE-agent to OpenHands (−6.7pp drop) while the LF oracle degrades significantly to 0.582 (−21.6pp)\n\nThe paper covers most of the experiments I'd anticipated from the review context. I'm wrapping up the remaining ablations and sensitivity analyses—cosine similarity threshold tuning, full-data confidence training, and the supplementary contrastive loss—before running the final parallel experiments.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14371,"cache_read_input_tokens":41357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14371},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sess